// Ch10 B11 "Why would they want to go down?" (E, 2 min). act2_ch10.md §2 B11. R09: dawn at the causeway
// gate, grey. Pell and Kerrid are where they were (Kerrid doesn't sleep; Pell, the Kirru way, stood). Asha
// goes straight to Pell and doesn't ask about his night (her tell is starting to stop). Pell answers a
// scene later, and this is the scene later: Ch9's "Which way should they point?" too. R10: Rhen and the
// blank shell, the question Ch9 left open. "My neck is very tired" is held back for Act III.
title: ch10_dawn_gate
location: ch10/reedhollow
---
@letterbox on
@fade in 2.0
@camera R09
@music reedhollow fade=3.0
@mark asha gate_asha walk
@wait 2.0
Asha [worried]: Pell. Why would the dead want to go down? #line:ch10_dawn_001
@wait 2.0
Pell [neutral]: They do not want to. You-people ask them. #line:ch10_dawn_002
Asha [sad]: ...And they come. #line:ch10_dawn_003
Pell [neutral]: You are very good at asking. #line:ch10_dawn_004 #tn:"Not a compliment and not an insult: a plain fact, gently said."
<<set $ch10_asha_asked_pell = true>>
@wait 1.5
@camera R10
@anim rhen look_at pell_shell
<<if $ch10_heard_ressa>>
    Rhen [neutral]: Your shell. They scraped it because of her. Ressa. #line:ch10_dawn_005
<<else>>
    Rhen [neutral]: Your shell. Why's it blank? #line:ch10_dawn_006
<<endif>>
@wait 1.5
Pell [neutral]: I did not turn around. #line:ch10_dawn_007
@wait 2.5
Pell [sad]: She went into the sea. I watched her go. Seventy years. #line:ch10_dawn_008
@wait 1.0
@mark pell root_walk_out walk
@mark toma line_2 walk
@mark asha line_3 walk
@mark ysolde line_4 walk
@mark liss line_5 walk
@mark rhen line_6 walk
@mark kerrid line_7 walk
@wait 3.0
<<set $ch10_complete = true>>
@letterbox off
@camera release
===
